Tark: @wiki opens the Wikipedia of the query's language. The URL has a new
`{tark:wikiLang}` replacement, filled from tark_xlit::WikipediaLanguage()
with the query's script and the user's accept-languages (SearchTermsArgs::
tark_accept_languages): Devanagari goes to the first Devanagari language the
user accepts (else Hindi), Tamil to Tamil, Latin to English. KeywordProvider,
SearchProvider, the transliteration rows (each puts its own language first)
and the controller's destination recompute all supply the languages.
search_engines depends only on the small //components/tark_xlit:languages
target. The starter pack data version is bumped so existing profiles get the
new @wiki URL.

